   write the same attribute and the map declares NO precedence among them,
   so max() picks arbitrarily -- BUT ONLY AMONG UNDISCRIMINATED WRITERS. A
   writer carrying a resolved `instance` or a declared `redundant_of` is
   SEPARATED, not competing: a nominee's name and a policyholder's name on
   one satellite are DIFFERENT ROWS. BOTH SCOPES are quoted below because a
   bare writer count overstates the arbitrariness -- on PARTY_FULL_NAME it
   overstates it nearly fivefold.
   DECLARED, NOT RESOLVED: choosing among same-run writers would invent an
   authority the map does not provide. NO CROSS-RUN DECISION REACHES THIS.
     AMBULANCE_TYPE                         opus_health_v2         2 writer(s), of which 2 UNDISCRIMINATED (0 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)  [same-table]
     TRANSPORT_ARRIVAL                      opus_health_v2         2 writer(s), of which 2 UNDISCRIMINATED (0 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)  [same-table]
     TRANSPORT_DEPARTURE                    opus_health_v2         2 writer(s), of which 2 UNDISCRIMINATED (0 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)  [same-table]
     TRANSPORT_PROVIDER_ADDRESS_TEXT        opus_health_v2         2 writer(s), of which 2 UNDISCRIMINATED (0 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)  [same-table]
     TRANSPORT_PROVIDER_CONTACT_NUMBER      opus_health_v2         2 writer(s), of which 2 UNDISCRIMINATED (0 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)  [same-table]
     TRANSPORT_PROVIDER_NAME                opus_health_v2         2 writer(s), of which 2 UNDISCRIMINATED (0 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)  [same-table]
